    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_49d977f2",
        "filename": "keystone/common/config.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 18338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-11T21:32:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would totally just take this out because it would be difficult to maintain.  Compliance standards will change overtime and how they are implemented can vary between operators.  Thus, I think we just want to give them options and then it would be up to them to say that the settings they have configured are compliant.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_a329259d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1030,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 1030,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fc85be5a8ca83eb9e7a56c2cb4f4337eb3d73bde",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_ef0dc68f",
        "filename": "keystone/common/config.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 6482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-12T01:58:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah okay, i see what you mean... how do you propose to solve the issue of deployers who don\u0027t want any PCI support? \n\nwe could change the defaults to None... but doesn\u0027t seem so great.\n\none negative about an \"enabled\" switch is that it\u0027s an all or nothing deal.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_49d977f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1030,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 1030,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fc85be5a8ca83eb9e7a56c2cb4f4337eb3d73bde",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_822e91a2",
        "filename": "keystone/common/config.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 18338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-12T02:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I think we do have to have some default values, but again, it\u0027s sort of up to operators to configure those setting to comply with PCI, HIPAA or any other standards.  The point being, is that they will now have options/settings they can configure to comply with those standards.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_ef0dc68f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1030,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 1030,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fc85be5a8ca83eb9e7a56c2cb4f4337eb3d73bde",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_5bfdb4af",
        "filename": "keystone/common/config.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1030,
      "author": {
        "id": 17579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-12T16:12:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll remove the option. I think the defaults are reasonable. If an operator has a problem with the compliance defaults they can change them. I agree with Ron since the enable option would be hard to maintain since the other config variables would have to reference the enable variable.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_822e91a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1030,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 1030,
        "endChar": 27
      },
